{:adr/id "2607142130"
 :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-1200 (tobacco products) operations-coordination coverage"
 :adr/status :accepted
 :adr/date "2026-07-14"
 :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :adr/related ["ADR-2607121000 (Wave 3 production/manufacturing actors)"
              "ADR-2607141200 (registry automation)"
              "cloud-itonami-isic-1200 repo docs/adr/0001-architecture.md"]

 :adr/context
 "ADR-2607121000 names tobacco products manufacturing (ISIC Rev.5 1200) as a
  Wave 3 production/manufacturing actor. Tobacco is regulated: excise-tax
  tracking, health-warning compliance, controlled-substance auditing required.
  The actor coordinates back-office workflow only: batch logging, maintenance
  scheduling, compliance escalation, shipment coordination. Processing-line
  equipment operation and regulatory certification remain human/operator
  exclusive. The existing :spec registry entry referenced a dead link
  (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-C1200). This ADR records the full implementation."

 :adr/decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-1200 as a tobacco-manufacturing back-office
  coordination actor following the established pattern (langgraph-clj
  StateGraph + independent Governor + Phase 0→3 rollout), with HARD
  INVARIANT: scope = coordination only, zero processing-line control or
  regulatory certification authority.

  Architecture:
  - TobaccoOpsAdvisor (sealed LLM): four proposal operations (:log-production-batch,
    :schedule-maintenance, :flag-compliance-concern, :coordinate-shipment)
  - TobaccoManufacturingGovernor: six HARD checks (spec-basis, evidence-complete,
    facility-permit-valid, batch-manifest-complete, compliance-concern-resolved,
    no-duplicates) + two SOFT escalations (low-confidence, high-stakes)
  - Phase gates 0→3: demo/pilot escalate; phase 2/3 commit if governor approves
  - Store protocol (MemStore dev/test, DatomicStore future)
  - Audit trail: every op logs :advised/:held/:committed facts

  HARD invariants:
  1. No processing-line equipment control (rooting, temperature, line speed)
  2. No regulatory certification (excise-tax, health-warning sign-off)
  3. No marketing or health claims
  4. Facility registration required (prevents unlicensed operations)"

 :adr/consequences
 {:positive ["Tobacco manufacturing workflow formally covered by cloud-itonami pattern"
             "Scope tight & explicit: coordination only, zero equipment or cert authority"
             "HARD check for unresolved compliance concerns prevents silent gaps"
             "Facility permit check ensures only licensed plants can log batches"
             "Complete audit trail for compliance & regulatory retrospective review"
             "High-stakes escalation ensures human sign-off for real actuations"
             "Phase gates allow cautious demo/pilot → supervised → full progression"]
  :negative ["No real-time monitoring of production-line conditions"
            "No integration with external excise-tax filing systems"
            "No integration with health-warning design systems"]}

